// Title: Created Files by Microsoft Sync Center
// Sigma ID: 409f8a98-4496-4aaa-818a-c931c0a8b832
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: elhoim
// Date: 2022-04-28 | Modified: 2022-06-02
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth, T1055, T1218, execution
// Description: This rule detects suspicious files created by Microsoft Sync Center (mobsync)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/intelligence-insights-november-2021/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_creation_by_mobsync.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\mobsync.exe" and (FolderPath endswith ".dll" or FolderPath endswith ".exe")
